From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown: Leave the flash writable
 with BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE

With BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE nothing is meant to protect the boot media,
yet the PCH lockdown still locks the empty SPI protected range
registers through DLOCK and sets BIOS Lock Enable. Intel's FPT checks
these bits and refuses to write the BIOS region with "Error 167:
Protected Range Registers are currently set by BIOS", although no
range is protected.

Skip the protected range lockdown and BIOS Lock Enable with
BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE. Without SMM write protection BLE only raises an
SMI when WPD is set, so no protection is lost. FLOCKDN, the BIOS
interface lock and the SPIBAR lock stay.

[Generated by Claude, an AI model by Anthropic.]

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown/lockdown.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown/lockdown.c b/src/soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown/lockdown.c
index ff7ca959..7b235ee0 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown/lockdown.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/pch/lockdown/lockdown.c
@@ -62,8 +62,9 @@ static void fast_spi_lockdown_cfg(int chipset_lockdown)
 	/* Set FAST_SPI opcode menu */
 	fast_spi_set_opcode_menu();
 
-	/* Discrete Lock Flash PR registers */
-	fast_spi_pr_dlock();
+	/* Discrete Lock Flash PR registers, unless the flash is meant to stay writable */
+	if (!CONFIG(BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE))
+		fast_spi_pr_dlock();
 
 	/* Check if SPI transaction is pending */
 	fast_spi_cycle_in_progress();
@@ -89,7 +90,8 @@ static void fast_spi_lockdown_cfg(int chipset_lockdown)
 		}
 
 		/* BIOS Lock */
-		fast_spi_set_lock_enable();
+		if (!CONFIG(BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE))
+			fast_spi_set_lock_enable();
 
 		/* EXT BIOS Lock */
 		fast_spi_set_ext_bios_lock_enable();
@@ -110,7 +112,8 @@ static void lpc_lockdown_config(int chipset_lockdown)
 		}
 
 		/* BIOS Lock */
-		lpc_set_lock_enable();
+		if (!CONFIG(BOOTMEDIA_LOCK_NONE))
+			lpc_set_lock_enable();
 	}
 }
 
